  "narrative": "All twelve due tests are direction +1 mean-difference claims, so positive signed estimates indicate that feature_020=1 is associated with less negative outcome_006 scores, i.e. weaker dependency. The conditional tests provide the most informative support for the global H96 lead. In the feature_060=0 stratum, H110 is strong and clinically large: +0.0881, 95% CI +0.0214 to +0.1548. In the feature_002=1 stratum, H114 is also strong: +0.0853, CI +0.0215 to +0.1492. The joint feature_002=0/feature_060=0 stratum H116 gives a very large point estimate, +0.1069, CI +0.0070 to +0.2067, but the exposed cell is only n=73 and the lower bound falls below a conservative practical threshold, so it is supportive rather than decisive. H111 within feature_060=1 and H113 within feature_002=0 are positive but imprecise, with intervals crossing null; they are compatible with the broader pattern but do not establish it. I therefore keep the strong conditionals unresolved and active pending validation rather than accepting subgroup associations that arise from post-hoc follow-up. The specificity panel is otherwise largely null: H109, H98, H100, H99, H101, and H102 have small estimates centered near null and do not support a broad weaker-dependency effect of feature_020. H97 is the closest borderline exception, with a negative signed estimate on outcome_012 (+1 direction; -0.0205, CI -0.0418 to +0.0007), suggesting possible opposite stronger dependency, but it is not clinically established and does not support the registered weaker-dependency direction. This mixed panel strengthens outcome_006 specificity but does not eliminate post-hoc or multiplicity concerns for the global H96 claim. I request independent validation of H96. If validation is positive with adequate magnitude and precision, acceptance of H96 and possibly the strongest conditionals will be reasonable; if validation fails, the feature_020/outcome_006 line should be closed or reduced to hypothesis-generating status. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associational statements, not causal effects or generalizable biology.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted set remains H15 only. H96 (outcome_006 feature_020 weaker-dependency direction) is the active lead and now has an independent validation request. Conditional outcome_006 tests are supportive but unresolved pending validation: H110 feature_060=0 +0.0881 [0.0214,0.1548]; H114 feature_002=1 +0.0853 [0.0215,0.1492]; H116 joint feature_002=0/feature_060=0 +0.1069 [0.0070,0.2067] but small cells. Weak positive conditionals H111 and H113 are deferred. Broad specificity panel rejects most other outcomes: H109, H97, H98, H99, H100, H101, H102 closed; H97 is borderline opposite for outcome_012 but below clinical threshold. If H96 validates, consider accepting H96 and reviewing H110/H114 as robust conditional claims; if H96 fails, close H96/H110/H114/H116 family or selectively validate H110 later. H112/H115, H103-H108, and H90 are deferred to preserve validation and analysis focus. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations."
